  "lapsed_date": "06/10/2029",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed change of use would result in the loss of Use Class E within Enfield Town Local Centre, without sufficient evidence to justify this loss, which in turn would undermine the objective of protecting employment uses (outside of the SIL or LSIS). Furthermore, the proposed development would result in an inappropriate conversion of floor space above commercial premises with the proposed development adversely affecting the appearance of the unit and shopping centre. The proposed development is thereby contrary to Policies CP13, CP19 and CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD22 and DMD30 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), in addition to the NPPF (2026).",
    "The proposed development, by reason of its inadequate floor to ceiling heights at second and loft floor levels would also give rise to the provision of substandard accommodation for occupiers of Bedrooms 3, 4, 5, 6 and and 7. The development is thereby contrary to Policies; D3 and D6 of the London Plan, CP 4 and CP 30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD 5, DMD 6, and DMD 8 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), in addition to the high-quality design aspirations set out within the NPPF (2026).",
    "The proposed development, by reason of its failure to provide any external amenity space for occupants of the HMO would give rise to substandard and inappropriate accommodation, incapable of meeting the reasonable needs of occupiers. The development is thereby contrary to Policies D3 and D6 of the London Plan (2021), CP 4 and CP 30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD 6, DMD 8 and DMD 9 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), in addition to the high-quality design aspirations set out within the NPPF (2026).",
    "The proposed roof extensions and alterations would appear as incongruous and unsympathetic additions to the host building and wider area, failing to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the Enfield Town Conservation Area, with the harm caused not being outweighed by any identified public benefits. The proposed development would thereby be contrary to Section 72(1) of the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990, Policies D3 and HC1 of the London Plan (2021), CP 30 and 31 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD13, DMD37 and DMD 44 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), in addition to the high-quality design aspirations set out within the NPPF (2026)."
  ],
